{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review the national planning policy framework to prevent excessive development",
        "additional_details": "Development should be distributed fairly and reduced where its cumulative impact on a community could be considered excessive in local communities.\r\n\r\nApproximately 1,600 homes are already being built around Leighton Hospital. An outline planning application has been submitted for approximately 2,100 homes at Weavers Green, and a further 1,700 homes are proposed at Leighton North. Taken together, these developments could add around 5,400 homes in and around the same area, fundamentally changing the scale and character of the affected communities.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to launch a review into the national planning framework, so housing targets reflect local infrastructure, the possible loss of countryside and housing developments already built, approved or proposed. ",
